&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director of Operational Excellence is responsible for establishing, optimizing, and overseeing the end-to-end quality assurance framework across all warehouse locations nationwide. This role leads the quality strategy, operational audits, cross-site process standardization, and warehouse project implementation to ensure accuracy, compliance, and operational excellence across the entire network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;：&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain the nationwide warehouse quality control strategy, policies, and operational standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and implement standardized operating procedures (SOPs), KPIs, and audit mechanisms for all warehouse functions, including receiving, putaway, inventory control, picking, packing, shipping, returns, and value-added services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze warehouse data to identify trends, gaps, and improvement opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct routine and random quality audits across all warehouse locations to ensure compliance with internal standards and customer requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and approve quality reports, deviation records, root-cause analyses, and corrective/preventative action plans (CAPA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead initiatives to improve order accuracy, inventory accuracy, packaging quality, and process compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Warehouse Operations, Supply Chain, HR/Training, Customer Service, and IT teams to ensure consistent implementation of quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate communication between site managers, regional leadership, and executive-level stakeholders regarding quality metrics and priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support client-facing teams by aligning warehouse quality processes with evolving customer requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead major warehouse quality improvement projects, multi-site rollouts, and technology/tool implementations, such as WMS enhancements and QC automation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure new processes, tools, and standards are deployed successfully across all locations and properly documented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver regular quality and operational performance reports to executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure adherence to relevant regulations, industry standards, and customer-specific SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audits as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other tasks as assigned by senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;：&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–10+ years of quality management experience in warehousing, logistics, or distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in multi-site quality leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual proficiency in Chinese is highly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of warehouse processes and quality methodologies (such as RCA, Lean, Six Sigma).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, leadership, and training capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to influence cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel nationwide as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with the Microsoft Office Suite and warehouse management systems (WMS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Job Type: Full-time, Onsite&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: Fontana, CA&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation: Starts at $150,000 per year, plus bonus&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Benefits: Medical/Dental/Vision Insurance, PTO, 401(k) Match&lt;/p&gt;

