&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About YQN:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;YQN is a fast-growing, technology-driven international logistics platform offering FCL, LCL, air freight, trucking, customs clearance, warehousing, and more. We are expanding our U.S. warehouse and transportation network and are looking for a Regional HR Business Partner to support our Northeast operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Port Reading, NJ, the Regional HRBP will be the strategic and hands-on HR partner for site leaders across our Northeast warehouse and transportation locations. This role drives workforce planning, employee relations, performance, compliance, and retention across a primarily frontline, multi-site workforce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary HR partner for regional and site leadership, aligning people strategy with operational goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead workforce planning with Operations, including headcount, staffing models, labor cost, and seasonal peaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage employee relations across sites: conduct and document workplace investigations, coach managers on corrective action, and resolve escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure HR practices comply with federal and state employment laws (including New Jersey and other Northeast state requirements), and partner with legal counsel as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze HR metrics such as turnover, attendance, time-to-fill, and engagement; recommend and drive action plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive retention and engagement programs for frontline and supervisory employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop site managers and supervisors on performance management, feedback, and people leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Recruiting on hiring plans for new sites and high-volume roles; support onboarding and new-site launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize HR policies, processes, and SOPs across sites in the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compensation reviews, promotions, and organizational changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of progressive HR experience, including 2+ years as an HRBP supporting multiple sites or a region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting frontline workforces in warehousing, logistics, distribution, or manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong employee relations and investigations experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of U.S. and New Jersey employment law; experience with other Northeast states is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data skills (Excel, HRIS reporting) and the ability to turn metrics into action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence and coach leaders in a fast-paced, changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel between sites up to 30%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mandarin speaking preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SHRM-CP/SHRM-SCP or PHR/SPHR is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location:&lt;/strong&gt; On-site in Port Reading, NJ, with regular travel to regional sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay:&lt;/strong&gt; $100,000 – $120,000 per year, based on experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; Medical/Dental/Vision Insurance, 401(K), PTO, Paid sick leave. Visa sponsorship available for qualified candidates.&lt;/p&gt;

