&lt;li&gt;Palletizing &amp;amp; Compliance Inspection: Inspect outbound pallet builds to ensure strict compliance with customer and platform routing guides (Amazon FBA, Walmart WFS, etc.). Enforce standards for pallet height limits, overhang restrictions, stretch-wrap gauge/tension, corner-board protection, and pallet-level UCC/shipping labels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dock Staging &amp;amp; Lane Management: Organize and maintain staging lanes by carrier, destination, and pickup appointment window. Verify pallet counts against pick tickets and WMS records to prevent mix-ups and short-shipments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trailer Loading &amp;amp; Weight Distribution: Direct and execute the loading of 53’ dry vans and ocean containers. Optimize cubic volume while ensuring proper front-to-back axle weight balancing. Supervise blocking, bracing, load bars, and airbag placement to eliminate freight shifting during transit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driver Coordination &amp;amp; Bill of Lading (BOL): Check in freight drivers, verify pickup authorizations (BOL/PRO/PO numbers), inspect trailer safety conditions (clean floor, no leaks), and ensure wheel chocks and dock locks are engaged. Review, confirm pallet counts, and obtain driver signatures for a clean BOL. Affix and record container seals when required.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;【Qualifications】&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;1.Experience: Minimum 1 year of warehouse outbound/dock shipping experience&lt;br&gt;2.Strong working knowledge of LTL/FTL operational workflows, common national/regional motor carriers (e.g., Estes, ODFL, R&amp;amp;L, TForce), and e-commerce wholesale shipping requirements.&lt;br&gt;3.Proficiency with WMS (Warehouse Management System), handheld RF scanners, and basic Microsoft Excel/Outlook.&lt;br&gt;4.Professional proficiency in Chinese speaking and reading is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
